    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP relies heavily on **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** today, as both anchor the top of our lineup with elite scores of 74.50 and 73.40, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** is a mandatory start against Brandon Woodruff; despite the pitcher's quality, the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and Woodruff's susceptibility to stolen bases makes **Corbin Carroll** an ideal candidate to capitalize on our league\u2019s priority for SB efficiency. Simultaneously, **Brice Turang** benefits from a massive SP skill boost against Merrill Kelly (5.47 xERA), and his projected #3 spot ensures he sees high-leverage at-bats in a favorable park environment. **Josh Naylor** (71.12) also demands attention; while the park factor is slightly negative, the matchup against Shane Bieber is too opportunistic to pass up, driving his efficiency well above the baseline.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Austin Riley**, whose score of 49.99 fell just shy of the active threshold. While **Austin Riley** offers pedigree, the optimizer favored the volume of **Max Muncy** (59.15) and **Seiya Suzuki** (65.20) due to their more favorable park factors and the specific platoon leverage against their respective opponents. **Mickey Moniak** (69.72) also warrants a high-conviction start despite a difficult platoon matchup against Robbie Ray; the significant park boost and his projected #2 spot in the order provide a statistical floor that outweighs the risk of the individual matchup.\n\nManagerial caution is advised regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as **Dalton Rushing** (47.03) and **Alex Freeland** (50.85) are currently tethered to bottom-tier lineup positions which suppress their daily utility. Furthermore, while we monitor our bench, both **Edwin Arroyo** and **Travis Bazzana** were left on the outside looking in, largely due to lingering 37-42% rain risks at their respective venues. We will maintain strict adherence to these efficiency thresholds to ensure our remaining game caps are utilized only on players like **James Wood** (52.66) and **Kyle Karros** (63.93), who are positioned to deliver immediate returns.",
